{"name":"Sage Advice","hex":"#948b76","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Wise.","Grave; serious; solemn."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very wise person or spiritual teacher; someone of gravity and wisdom, especially, a teacher venerable for years, and of sound judgment and prudence; a grave or stoic philosopher."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sage"},{"term":"advice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An opinion offered to guide behavior in an effort to be helpful.","Deliberate consideration; knowledge."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Misspelling of advise."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sage (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Sage is a grey-green resembling that of dried sage leaves. As a quaternary color, it is an equal mix of the tertiary colors citron and slate. The hex RGB color value of the adjacent sage swatch is BCB88A. For decades, some military flight jackets were made in sage green."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Sage_iPhone_17.jpg/330px-Sage_iPhone_17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sage_(color)","wikidata":"Q7399114"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"sage":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/79/En-us-sage.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/79/En-us-sage.ogg/En-us-sage.ogg.mp3"}],"advice":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/ff/En-us-advice.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/ff/En-us-advice.ogg/En-us-advice.ogg.mp3"}]}}}